meta {
  name: Watch events
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/games/{{gameId}}/events
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{guestToken}}
}

docs {
  Hold a stream open and receive every state the game reaches.
  
  Bruno collects the whole body before it shows anything, so this request proves that the
  token opens the stream, but it does not show views as they arrive. To watch a game, use
  curl in a second terminal instead:
  
      curl -N "localhost:8080/api/v1/games/<id>/events?token=<token>"
  
  The stream also accepts the token in the query string, because a browser EventSource
  cannot set a header. A query string reaches logs and proxy history, so the header is the
  better of the two places wherever a client can use it.
}
